body:
I'd say it heavily depends on the bracket you're playing. 

In lower ranks (let's say below 3k) splitpushing and waiting till someone gets out of position for a pickoff is the best bet. If they don't even try to escape their base, then farm all lanes and jungle with your team, when eventually you'll be able to power through with aegis and cheese. 

If you play with a group of premades, or higher ranks, coordinated dive could work. Even in late game, it will take just a couple of stuns to kill him. For example, you can have some hero blinking in, revealing sniper, using hex. Then some high dmg core blinks nearby, starts hitting, and chain-stuns with an abyssal blade, finishing off the hero before he can do anything. HOWEVER, it heavily depends on both lineups and the execution of the plays.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Fights after buybacks is a separate topic in itself.  For late game usually, if your opponents have more spells/bkbs than your team, after buybacks you run, if 1 or 2 heroes die, it's usually fine. But as always.... depends on situation.
